---
# karakeep's search index. karakeep dials it at MEILI_ADDR=http://karakeep-meilisearch:7700
# (deployment.yaml.j2), and nothing else does.
#
# THIS POLICY SHIPS WITH THE ROLE THAT NEEDS IT. It lived in roles/k8s/netpol-baseline/ until
# 2026-09-10, one role away from the Deployment whose pod cannot start without it (#1620, the
# same split as authelia's session store in #1609). The warrant here is the POD SPEC rather
# than the app: karakeep itself degrades when meilisearch is unreachable — it logs search
# errors and serves — but deployment.yaml.j2's `wait-for-deps` initContainer retries
# karakeep-meilisearch:7700 in an UNBOUNDED loop, so with this policy absent the pod sits in
# Init forever, with no restart count to read and no CrashLoopBackOff to notice.
# `build_k8s_dep_map` cannot see a split like it — it derives a role's edges from templates
# inside that role's own directory (ansible/filter_plugins/toposort.py), so a dependency
# expressed in a sibling role produces no edge and no ordering constraint to violate.
# ansible/tests/services/test_karakeep_backend_policies.py pins the co-location.
#
# 7700 is the containerPort AND the Service port — verified 2026-08-20, they match, and that
# same test keeps them matching.
#
# NO `netpol_baseline_enforced` BRANCH, unlike netpol-baseline's own policies. That lever is a
# role default of netpol-baseline, and Ansible role defaults are role-scoped: it does not
# resolve here, and `| default(true)` would read as honouring the lever while ignoring it.
# Dropping it is also the right behaviour rather than a concession — the lever exists to
# restore reachability in a rollback, and the only path that reaches meilisearch at all is the
# one this file grants, so leaving it on cannot be what an operator is rolling back from.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: karakeep-meilisearch
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: karakeep-meilisearch
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: karakeep
      ports:
        - port: 7700
          protocol: TCP
